 "answer": "Version 0.124.0 added support for comma-separated values that act as OR conditions in `--filter-metadata`.\n\nThe release notes say: \"support comma-separated OR values in --filter-metadata\" [promptfoo/0.124.0.md].\n\nThe CLI docs describe how it works: \"Filter tests by metadata substring. Commas separate OR values (`\\,` is a comma); repeated flags use AND.\" [promptfoo/site/docs/usage/command-line.md]\n\nSo a single flag can now take something like `category=math,science`. That matches tests with either value, and `\\,` stands for a literal comma. Repeating the flag still combines filters with AND.",
